US-047 is still **Partial**. I did not emit a completion signal, because the renderer half of the story is not built.

**What exists:** the CPU terrain runtime in `engine/world` and its 14 fixture cases, plus a render bridge (`engine/render/src/terrain_mesh.cpp`) that turns each tile into a validated `MeshData` with a per-vertex splat channel. The progress log records the earlier gate results for that CPU work.

**What's missing:**
- **Terrain in the frame.** Tiles are not drawn. The clean route is an ECS entity with a renderable component whose mesh comes from `upload_mesh`. That gives depth and shadows through the existing static path.
- **Splat shading.** The static vertex layout (`pack_vertices`, `scene.hlsl`) has no splat attribute. Adding one to every mesh would be wrong, so it needs a terrain-only layout.
- **RT.** Heightfield terrain is still reported unsupported in `rt_effects_geometry_support()`.
- **GPU fixture and bench.** The tile coverage and LOD-switch test on DX12 and Vulkan, and the `engine_bench` workload, have not been written.
- **Gates.** The Windows GPU and bench gates have not been run. WSL has no Vulkan device, so the GPU parts can only be verified through a Windows run.

**Decision I made:** vertex colour for the splat weights, as a terrain-only layout. The tile mesh already carries normalised weights per vertex.

I did not edit renderer code this pass. Those changes touch `scene_renderer.cpp` (3,783 lines), `scene.hlsl`, and the RT surface set, and I could not verify them here. I appended a survey entry to `.ralph-tui/progress.md` with the integration point and the status. The next pass should start with the terrain entity path in extraction, then the splat layout, then the GPU fixture on Windows.
